  "_comment": "nice_ron's SOUND v1 — melodic techno gone 8-BIT, 140, E minor. The arc: peaceful meadow (bells + pad on the e-g-b-a cell, deer on screen) → THE SNEEZE → 'nice one, ron' → a SHORT four-on-floor techno drop wrapped in melody (offbeat technobass walks the cell, droplead sings it; sneezestab punches bar 1s; drop II is a dialog: sneezechop argues on odd bars, ronstab answers 'nice ron' twice on evens; the machine sections are square+crush chiptune, the meadow stays organic) → the confession → the apology → stillness. One voice at a time. Speech cuts peak-normalized to -3dB (source is quiet phone audio); gains sit at ~0.7-1.0 against that. Moves spent from the bank: one-riff economy + filter-as-energy (switch-angel); riff banks + pick walk, inhabit rhythm/harmony split, four-bass pyramid, @ drop-hold, postgain-after-crush (oazoor). Drop basses are 4 skeletons over one E-minor chord bank; drop I walks <0 1 0 2>, drop II <2 1 2 3> ending held.",
